From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: BlackF1re <55582873+BlackF1re@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 00:45:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: soc: qcom: saw2: describe CPU memory supply

The MSM8226 shared CPU SAW regulator must raise the PMIC memory supply
before raising the CPU voltage. Describe that supply dependency so boards
can connect their existing RPM-controlled memory rail.

Signed-off-by: BlackF1re <55582873+BlackF1re@users.noreply.github.com>
---
diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/soc/qcom/qcom,saw2.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/soc/qcom/qcom,saw2.yaml
index c2f1f5946..74b2418b9 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/soc/qcom/qcom,saw2.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/soc/qcom/qcom,saw2.yaml
@@ -53,6 +53,9 @@ properties:
       - description: Base address and size of the alias register region
     minItems: 1
 
+  vdd-mx-supply:
+    description: Memory rail tracking the MSM8226 shared CPU voltage.
+
   regulator:
     $ref: /schemas/regulator/regulator.yaml#
     description: Indicates that this SPM device acts as a regulator device
